# {{.Name}}

A command line tool built on [mizu](https://github.com/go-mizu/mizu)'s `console`
package.

## Running it

```
go mod tidy
go run . greet ada
go run . greet --loud ada
go run . --help
```

## Testing it

```
go test ./...
```

A command is tested by calling it, not by starting a process. `consoletest`
gives it streams it can read back and returns what it wrote along with the code
it would have exited with, so a test is a function call.

## What is here

```
main.go       the app, and the one command on it
main_test.go  a test for each way that command can be run
go.mod        the module
```

Every command is a struct with a `Spec` and a `Run`. The fields are where its
flags and arguments parse into, which is why `Run` takes nothing beyond the
context and the streams. Adding a command means adding a struct and a line in
`newApp`.

Every command also takes `--verbose`, `--quiet`, `--json`, `--color`,
`--no-color`, `--no-interaction` and `--timeout` without declaring them.
